  "_classes_why": "vowels only: a closure or a fricative is one shape at one opening (MBP must be shut, FV must bite); his Uh/Ah/Aa included (round 41).",
  "k": 3,
  "_k_why": "the v2 desk harvest (clip-v2-talk-pause, 289 f, 25 words) gives 4-14 same-shape candidates per vowel at shape_gate 0.12; three openings use them without repeating a frame.",
  "pad": 1,
  "_pad_why": "the speller's classes split a word's span evenly, not by phoneme; one frame either side takes the vowel's edges without reaching the next word (words are 4-8 f on this take).",
  "shape_gate": 0.12,
  "_shape_gate_why": "measured 2026-10-24 on the v2 desk contact sheet: at 0.25 the EH set took a lip-bite frame and the OH set an EE smile; at 0.12 every row is one shape at three openings; at 0.08 ER and WOO had under three candidates.",
  "min_spread": 1.3,
  "_min_spread_why": "a class whose widest variant opens under 1.3x its quietest has nothing to vary (Ah measured 0.108-0.119 = 1.10x, one tile); the rest measure 1.43-3.8x at gate 0.12.",
  "min_open_of_anchor": 0.4,
  "_min_open_why": "with no floor the EE and AH sets took near-shut transition frames (lip 0.010, 0.015 against anchors 0.094, 0.115); a vowel is never shut, so the quietest is at least 0.4x the picked opening.",
  "within": false,
  "_within_why": "false = one variant per note, ranked on the note's mean loudness; true = re-ranked at every hop. Set from the SyncNet A/B on :8116."
 },
